course: dictionary
lesson: 5782
title: A strong chemical: lye
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Lye is a very strong chemical. Scientists call it an alkali, and it is used to make soap and to clean drains.
explain: «Long ago people made soap by boiling fat with lye from wood ash.» The clues are soap and wood ash, so lye must be something you add to fat to change it into soap.
explain: Lye can burn your skin and eyes badly, so it is dangerous. The sentence «a very harsh alkali, so not a kitchen experiment» tells you it must never be tried at home.
fact: Lye is an alkali, a very strong chemical.
fact: Lye is used to make soap and to clean drains.
fact: «Caustic» means able to burn or eat away at things, like skin.
fact: Long ago, soap was made by boiling fat with lye from wood ash.
fact: Lye can burn skin and eyes badly, so it must be kept locked away and never touched.
exercise: «Lye» is a very strong chemical. What kind of chemical is lye? | *A strong alkali | A sweet sugar | A weak, harmless drink
exercise: «Long ago people made soap by boiling fat with lye from wood ash.» What was lye used to make? | Paper | *Soap | Bread
exercise: Why must lye be kept locked away? | It floats on water | It tastes very sweet | *It can burn skin and eyes badly | It makes plants grow faster
test: «Caustic» lye can burn skin. What does caustic suggest? | Able to float on water | Sweet to taste | Very cold | *Able to burn or eat away at things
test: Which statement about lye is true? | It is a kind of fruit juice | It is a gentle food for babies | It is safe to touch with bare hands | *It is a strong alkali used to make soap
exam: If lye gets into your eye, what should you do? | *Tell an adult at once and get help straight away | Eat something to help it pass | Rub it hard with your hand | Ignore it, because it will pass
